# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# HTML keeps Cloudflare's default, Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate,
# so a new deploy shows up straight away.
#
# CSS, JS and fonts get a content hash in their file names at build time
# (scripts/lib/hash-assets.mjs) and images from eleventy-img are hashed too, so a
# changed file always has a new URL and these can be cached for a year.
# Other files (PDFs, the favicon) keep their names, so they use the default.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/js/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/assets/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/img/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
